# Components

A component is a function that takes props and returns HTML. This one
greets whoever you pass as `name`:

```rocci
import Html

@component
Hello = |{ name }|
    <p>Hello, <strong>{name}</strong></p>
```

```sh
rocci view Hello.rocci --component Hello --arg name=Ada
```

The window should read **Hello, Ada**. HTTP declarations in the same file
are ignored during `view`.

The cataloged module with scoped CSS is
[Styling.rocci](/examples/styling/source/Styling-rocci/).

## Call another component

Names are PascalCase. Consecutive leading capitals (`HTMLShell`) are
rejected; write `HtmlShell`. Nested markup is a second `Html` argument,
not a `children` field. Putting `Html` in the props record wraps it in
`Html.text` and escapes it.

```rocci
@component Card = |{ title }, content|
    <section>
        <h2>{title}</h2>
        {content}
    </section>

@component Page = |_|
    <Card title="Hello">
        <p>Body is Html, not a string.</p>
    </Card>
```

A self-closing tag is a one-argument call. Qualified calls use the
imported module: `<Design.Button />` becomes `Design.button`. Missing
PascalCase names fail in Roc, not in a client-side registry.

`??` field defaults are **experimental**. Omit the field at the call
site; generated Roc uses a type-position default so Roc fills it.

A component is **pure**: given the same props and body, it produces the
same markup. It cannot log, open SQLite, or read the request. Effects
belong in `@init` and handlers. There is no runtime component registry
and no implicit instance state.

## Preview with fixtures

`@fixture` bindings feed `rocci view` and `rocci browse`. `@test`
bindings check a boolean with `rocci test`. Neither changes the generated
component function.

```rocci
@fixture{target: Hello}
helloTest = { name: "Ada" }
```

```sh
rocci view Hello.rocci --component Hello
```

The preview shows **Hello, Ada** from `helloTest`. Pass `--arg name=Roc`
to override.

Put reusable widgets in `components/`. Keep page-private helpers in the
same `.rocci` module. `rocci browse components/` lists fixtures across a
directory.

The exact grammar is in
[Components](/docs/reference/language/components/).

